Exabeam Plug-in Forge — Terms

This repository contains both proprietary and open-source components.

Proprietary components are governed by the Exabeam Enterprise Agreement:

    https://www.exabeam.com/legal/enterprise-agreement/

The terms are maintained at that address and are not reproduced here. Use of a
plugin distributed here is subject to the same terms of use as the Exabeam
products it works with.

Open-source components retain the license declared in their own directory.

The full mapping:

  - Vendored plugin payloads (one directory per plugin, for example soc/).
    Each carries its own LICENSE and NOTICE, which state the terms of that
    plugin as distributed here. An SPDX-License-Identifier header on a file
    inside a payload states the license of the open-source software that
    plugin includes; that software stays under that license inside the
    distribution, and its license text ships with the plugin (for example
    soc/LICENSE-APACHE).

  - overlays/, and the identity and license files applied by
    scripts/vendor_plugin.py. Proprietary, and licensed under the Exabeam
    Enterprise Agreement.

  - The catalog tooling under scripts/ carries SPDX-License-Identifier headers
    and is licensed as those headers state.

  - Everything else in this repository. Proprietary, and licensed under the
    Exabeam Enterprise Agreement.

